<h2>Presenter window, notes and tools</h2>

<p>
  Press <b>p</b>: a second window shows your notes (the HTML comments), the next slide and a timer.
  It stays in sync with the audience window, both ways — you can drive from either.
</p>

<p>
  On the slide itself: <b>l</b> a laser pointer, <b>d</b> draw (<b>c</b> clears, <b>Esc</b> stops), <b>z</b> a 2× magnifier,
  <b>a</b> autoplay (or <c>"autoplay": 5</c> in <c>deck.json</c>, <c>?autoplay=5</c> in the URL). A slide with <c>hidden: true</c>
  in its <c><slide></c> block is skipped in the show and the PDF.
</p>

<code lang=typescript>
  // the presenter view lists the HTML comments of the current slide
  const notes = slide.notes;
</code>

<notes>
  Like this one. Every HTML comment in a slide becomes one paragraph of notes.
</notes>
